00:34:25.220 --> 00:34:29.920
And we're gonna take this show to the next level by doing the Essential Games List.

00:34:33.280 --> 00:34:37.000
Yeah, so I mean, like, look, there's some great humor in presentation here.

00:34:37.320 --> 00:34:40.680
I like... I do...

00:34:40.680 --> 00:34:45.040
You know, contrary to what I was saying about the actual, like, way cavemen talk, of which,

00:34:45.120 --> 00:34:46.460
of course, I'm a caveman apologist.

00:34:47.200 --> 00:34:51.200
You know, like, the actual theming of the events and everything is fantastic.

00:34:51.840 --> 00:34:58.360
Um, the over-the-top animations and, uh, the various reactions that you can have by failing

00:34:58.360 --> 00:35:00.820
or winning these events is great.

00:35:01.000 --> 00:35:07.320
It's, you know, the replayability of it all is probably limited into how much enjoyment

00:35:07.320 --> 00:35:08.200
you get out of this.

00:35:08.340 --> 00:35:12.220
I think that's what I was also trying to get out of with, like, the main mode being doing

00:35:12.220 --> 00:35:14.340
the entire Ugglympics.

00:35:14.580 --> 00:35:20.160
But realistically, the actual replayability is just, well, I'm really good at the, um,

00:35:20.920 --> 00:35:22.820
you know, at the Sabretooth Tiger race.

00:35:22.920 --> 00:35:26.500
So I'm just gonna do that. Which is actually kind of funny to be good at that one because that's the one that's,

00:35:26.580 --> 00:35:29.160
like, the least, like, I could improve upon.

00:35:29.360 --> 00:35:35.360
Like, at least the other ones are, like, measuring something of, like, how many, uh, foots you, uh,

00:35:35.360 --> 00:35:39.200
you got across, uh, or, or how high you vaulted.

00:35:39.540 --> 00:35:45.680
All that to say, it's not that I think, it's not that I think that they even made a bad game

00:35:45.680 --> 00:35:49.340
here. I think I was, like, thinking that when I first started playing this game, just, like,

00:35:49.400 --> 00:35:52.200
wow, I really don't have any appetite to play this kind of game.

00:35:52.540 --> 00:35:58.020
Uh, I've, I've seen a lot of these track and field style games already on the NES, and

00:35:58.020 --> 00:36:02.320
now this one's just caveman themed, which is, like, for me, never go back to the past,

00:36:02.340 --> 00:36:03.200
always go to the future.

00:36:03.200 --> 00:36:06.240
I'd rather have, like, some cyberpunk games or something.

00:36:07.060 --> 00:36:13.240
But the actual just downfall of the game for me was just in how, like, just in how little

00:36:13.820 --> 00:36:17.080
I'm going to think about this game again after the fact.

00:36:17.360 --> 00:36:23.700
Like, these, all these things, whether they're good minigames or not, just takes, like, very

00:36:23.700 --> 00:36:26.400
little, like, to, to enjoy.

00:36:26.920 --> 00:36:29.860
And therefore, it was not, like, even though I was joking about, like, yeah, I'm gonna show

00:36:29.860 --> 00:36:33.300
people this. It's like, yeah, I'm realistically never gonna show anybody this.

00:36:33.380 --> 00:36:38.280
And I can't put a game on the essential games list that I don't even, like, think is, like,

00:36:38.380 --> 00:36:39.800
worth showing off.

00:36:39.940 --> 00:36:41.760
So, no. Caveman games, not for me.

